'''John Francis Gillen Sr.'''<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Through the tunnel: senior has fond memories |url=https://247sports.com/college/wisconsin/Article/Through-the-tunnel-senior-has-fond-memories-104140432/ |access-date=2022-03-10 |website=Badger247 |language=en-US}}</ref> (born November 5, 1958) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[linebacker]] for the [[History of the St. Louis Cardinals (NFL)|St. Louis Cardinals]] and [[New England Patriots]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL), as well as the [[Chicago Blitz]] and the [[Arizona Outlaws]] of the [[United States Football League]] (USFL).<ref>{{Cite web |title=John Gillen football Statistics on StatsCrew.com |url=https://www.statscrew.com/football/stats/p-gillejoh001 |access-date=2022-03-10 |website=www.statscrew.com |language=en}}</ref> He played [[college football]] for the [[Illinois Fighting Illini football|Illinois Fighting Illini]].<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=John Gillen Stats |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/G/GillJo20.htm |access-date=2022-03-10 |website=Pro-Football-Reference.com |language=en}}</ref>
